course: dictionary
lesson: 3968
title: Fussy: hard to please
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one fits. Fussy is a good example. Look at the words around it and ask what would fit there.
explain: «Very fussy eaters may miss some nutrients, so a doctor may suggest a multivitamin.» A fussy eater only likes certain foods, so fussy here means only wanting certain things. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Toad complains about «the pettifogging mistrustfulness of paid officials». Pettifogging means fussy about small things, so the officials worry too much about tiny details. Old words also help: «don't be particular» means «don't be fussy».
explain: Fussy can describe a person, a baby, or a thing. Ask yourself: is someone hard to please, is a baby cranky, or is something covered in too many decorations? Then check that your meaning fits the sentence.
fact: Fussy means hard to please, and caring too much about small details.
fact: A fussy eater only likes certain foods.
fact: Fussy can also describe something with too many decorations or details.
fact: A fussy baby is cranky and keeps crying.
fact: «Not fussy» means happy with anything.
exercise: «Very fussy eaters may miss some nutrients.» What does fussy mean here? | *Only liking certain foods | Eating very quickly | Being very tall | Liking every food in the shop
exercise: Nadia says, «Don't be fussy, just eat it.» What does fussy mean? | Full of fun and games | Very quiet and calm | *Hard to please and too careful about small things | Quick and rushed
exercise: «The fussy baby cried all night.» What does fussy describe? | Clean and tidy | Happy and laughing | *Cranky and crying | Calm and sleepy
test:
«The cake was covered in fussy pink icing and tiny sugar flowers.» What does fussy mean here? | Plain and simple | *Covered in too many decorations and details | Cold and hard | Sweet and sour
Which phrase means happy with anything? | Fussy about | Very fussy | *Not fussy | Fussy eater
exam: Which sentence uses fussy to mean hard to please? | She fussy bought a bun from the shop. | The fussy rain fell softly on the hill. | *Mum is fussy and won't let us leave until every small thing is perfect. | The fussy river ran quickly to the sea.
